        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Walton, John Wooden\n- Organizations: UCLA Bruins, UCLA, NCAA\n- Roles: Head coach, College Player of the Year\n- Events: Division I national titles, NCAA national championships\n\nFacts:\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton became known for playing for John Wooden's UCLA Bruins powerhouse team.\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton won three successive College Player of the Year Awards.\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton led the UCLA Bruins to two Division I national titles.\n- John Wooden was nicknamed the \"Wizard of Westwood.\"\n- As head coach at UCLA, John Wooden won ten NCAA national championships in a 12-year period.\n- As head coach at UCLA, John Wooden won a record seven consecutive NCAA national championships.",
